Goal:-  This lab has an admin panel at /admin, which identifies administrators using a forgeable cookie. Solve the lab by accessing the admin panel and using it to delete the user carlos

Observation:- admin pannel is accessed by changing the role using burpsuit

Steps to solve :- 

        Step1:- Access the lab
        Step2:- Login Using given credential
        Step3:- while moving to "my account" change the request using burpsuit 
        step4:- change isadmin from false to true 
        Step5:- Delete user name Carlos

Result:- Access to admin pannel and we can add or delete user from the database

Root Cause:-1) The application identifies administrator privileges using a client-side cookie that can be modified by the user.

            2) There is no server-side validation of user roles or privileges.

            3) Authorization decisions are based on untrusted user input, allowing privilege escalation by changing isadmin=false to isadmin=true

Fix:-  Enforce server-side authorization and use signed session mechanisms instead of trusting client-side role values.
